Description-Content-Type: text/markdown

# BridgeIDS — Bridging Legacy IDS and Modern IIoT Security

**Cross-dataset transfer learning · domain adaptation · continual learning · zero-shot detection · NLP interlingua ·
explainable AI · drift analysis · dynamic (streaming) detection · Power BI**

```
NSL-KDD (legacy, connections) ──► ForgeIIoT (bridge, MQTT IIoT packets) ──► Edge-IIoTset (modern IIoT packets)
```

The project implements the full two-team plan (`docs/img/project_plan.jpg`) and extends it. It answers RQ1–RQ5 plus
**RQ6: does dynamic, adaptive detection recover performance after a domain shift?** Dataset records are replayed as
real network packets (UDP / TCP / HTTP / MQTT) into a live, explainable and self-adapting detector.

## Key results (from `results/tables`, seed 42)

| Question | Finding |
|---|---|
| RQ1 legacy → modern | NSL-KDD model on Edge-IIoTset: ROC-AUC **0.583** (near chance); Edge → NSL is inverted (AUC 0.253), a sign of concept drift |
| RQ2 bridge | ForgeIIoT → Edge-IIoTset: AUC **0.853** (CBS), F1 0.950 (PBS); proxy-A-distance 1.44 (Forge–Edge) vs 1.97 (NSL–Edge); concept shift 0.035 vs 0.386 |
| RQ3 domain adaptation | helps only where concepts are shared (CORAL +0.055 AUC NSL→Forge, DomainNorm +0.037 Forge→Edge); cannot fix NSL→Edge |
| NLP interlingua | Forge → NSL AUC 0.340 → **0.787**; NSL → Edge 0.583 → 0.714 (numeric → text / numeric+text) |
| Continual learning | EWC+Replay final balanced acc **0.857** (naive 0.744), BWT +0.148 |
| RQ5 zero-shot | never-seen Edge INJECTION detected at **98%** using only benign target traffic (benign FPR 10%); DAP names unseen classes 58% vs 25% chance |
| RQ4 XAI | SHAP ranking agreement Forge–Edge ρ=**0.62**, NSL–Forge ρ=-0.03; explanations reveal the same shift |
| RQ6 static → dynamic | after a Forge→Edge shift: MCC 0.618 (static) → **0.864** (dynamic, 10% feedback), FPR 0.58 → 0.22; drift flagged 1128 packets after the switch |
| Leakage audit | ForgeIIoT fine-grained accuracy 69.4% leak-free vs **99.9%** with frame.number/epoch/tcp.stream, which explains the earlier notebook's "100%" |

![live dashboard](docs/img/dashboard_live.png)


## Quick start

| | Windows | Linux / macOS |
|---|---|---|
| install | `setup_windows.bat` | `./setup_linux.sh` |
| all experiments + paper + dashboards | `run_all.bat` | `./run_all.sh` |
| live demo | `demo_stream.bat campaign edge` | `./demo_stream.sh campaign edge` |

Detailed guides: [`docs/SETUP_WINDOWS.md`](docs/SETUP_WINDOWS.md) · [`docs/SETUP_LINUX.md`](docs/SETUP_LINUX.md).
Python 3.10–3.13, CPU only (no CUDA or PyTorch: a small numpy NN engine provides the MLP, DANN and EWC).

The zip already contains the prepared dataset samples (`data/processed`), trained live-detector models
(`results/models`) and all results, so everything works without downloading the raw data again.

## Commands

```bash
python -m bridgeids.run prepare [--force]        # raw data -> data/processed/*.parquet
python -m bridgeids.run exp all                  # experiments 01-12 (or: exp 03 05 08)
python -m bridgeids.run report                   # reports/paper_draft.md, reports/results_dashboard.html, powerbi/data
python -m bridgeids.run serve [--artifacts bench_forge_only]   # live detector  http://127.0.0.1:8000
python -m bridgeids.run replay --scenario campaign|zero_day|domain_shift|shuffle \
                               --dataset edge|forge|nsl --rate 400 --transport udp|tcp|http|mqtt
```

## What is in the box

| Experiment | Plan item | Main outputs (`results/tables`, `results/figures`) |
|---|---|---|
| 01 dataset study + taxonomy | T1-1, T2-2 | `e01_dataset_statistics`, `e01_attack_relationship_matrix` |
| 02 baselines (DT, RF, AdaBoost, XGB, LGBM, MLP) + **leakage audit** | T1-3 | `e02_baselines_binary`, `e02_leakage_audit` |
| 03 cross-dataset testing / domain-shift report | T1-4, RQ1, RQ2 | `e03_domain_shift_report`, `e03_cbs_matrix_roc_auc.png` |
| 04 transfer learning (0.02–10 % target labels) | T1-5 | `e04_transfer_learning_results`, `e04_transfer_curves.png` |
| 05 domain adaptation (DomainNorm, CORAL, TCA, IW, self-training, DANN) | T1-6, RQ3 | `e05_domain_adaptation` |
| 06 continual learning (naive, EWC, replay, EWC+replay, GBM, joint) | T1-7 | `e06_continual_learning`, `e06_continual_matrices.png` |
| 07 NLP representation / language interlingua | T2-3 | `e07_nlp_cross_dataset`, `e07_text_embedding_map.png` |
| 08 zero-shot (leave-family-out, cross-dataset, DAP, text ZSL) | T2-4, RQ5 | `e08_zeroshot_*`, `e08_semantic_zsl` |
| 09 XAI (SHAP, LIME, explanation drift, narratives) | T2-5, RQ4 | `e09_*` |
| 10 drift (KL, JS, Wasserstein, PSI, MMD, proxy-A, concept, attack) | T2-6 | `e10_drift_summary` |
| 11 static vs dynamic detection under domain shift | RQ6 | `e11_stream_benchmark`, `e11_stream_static_vs_dynamic.png` |
| 12 live-detector models, Weka J48/RF/AdaBoostM1, Power BI export | T1-3, T2-7 | `e12_weka_results`, `powerbi/data` |

Also included:

* **Research write-ups:** `reports/paper_draft.md` (auto-generated with live numbers), `reports/related_work.md` (44 papers, 2023–2026), `reports/results_dashboard.html`.
* **Plan audit:** `docs/PLAN_COVERAGE.md` covers what the previous team delivered, what was fixed and what was added, plus the improved plan.
* **Architecture:** `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
* **Power BI kit:** `powerbi/POWERBI_GUIDE.md` with DAX measures, theme, Power Query script, star-schema CSVs and three real-time options.
* **Weka:** ARFF exports and scripts in `weka/`.
* **Walkthrough notebook:** `notebooks/BridgeIDS_walkthrough.ipynb`; the original hand-over notebooks are kept in `notebooks/handover_original`.

## Project layout

```
configs/default.yaml        all paths, sample sizes, seeds, stream settings
src/bridgeids/
  data/        loaders.py (NSL txt/arff, Forge raw captures, Edge) · taxonomy.py (7 super-classes, attributes, descriptions)
  features/    views.py   canonical view -> CBS (all datasets) / PBS (Forge<->Edge) / native leak-free
  models/      zoo.py (baselines) · npnet.py (numpy MLP, DANN+GRL, exact Fisher/EWC) · hybrid.py (zero-day hybrid)
  adaptation/  methods.py (DomainNorm, CORAL, TCA, importance weighting, self-training)
  nlp/         flow2text.py (interlingua) · encoders.py (SBERT or offline TF-IDF+LSA)
  xai/         explain.py (SHAP, LIME, rank agreement, narratives)
  drift.py     KL / JS / Wasserstein / PSI / MMD / proxy-A / concept shift / stream PSI
  stream/      replayer.py · engine.py · server.py (FastAPI, UDP/TCP/HTTP/MQTT, WebSocket) · static/dashboard.html
  experiments/ e01 … e12
  reporting/   plots.py · powerbi.py · report.py
  run.py       CLI
data/raw (NSL-KDD included) · data/processed (prepared samples) · results/ · reports/ · powerbi/ · weka/ · docs/ · tests/
```

## Datasets and citation
* NSL-KDD — Tavallaee et al., IEEE CISDA 2009.
* ForgeIIoT / IIEST_IoTForge_Pro — P. Kumar, S. Mullick, R. Das, IEEE DataPort, doi:10.21227/c4z1-yc52.
* Edge-IIoTset — M. A. Ferrag et al., IEEE Access 10:40281–40306, 2022, doi:10.1109/ACCESS.2022.3165809.
